{"ts":"2026-08-31T11:51:34.834Z","author":"pi-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.2:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"5a7430c457633e76d82d3790","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.2:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-31T11:51:34.834Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-08-31T11:51:34.834Z","author":"pi-agent","text":"Fix: Replaced 'exit 0' inside the retry loop with 'bun_succeeded=1; break'. The loop now terminates normally on success via break, and the step exits after the loop based on the success flag: 'if (( ! bun_succeeded )); then exit 1; fi'. The probe returns status to loop-level termination rather than exiting the step from within the loop. Revert-proof: test 'a probe called from inside a retry loop must only return status, not exit the step from within the loop' fails RED when exit 0 is restored inside the loop body."}]}],"before_hash":"d22514255bc9a3771e4b7ed4b423cdbeb3cdc235688f964b7f1ddab09c94d8c2","after_hash":"d62555d817e079131bc55a3efb8144a880299b55ab386c7a403f9404d2b85b46","item_hash_version":2}
